==Strategy==
The problem most players face in this stage are the Pure Gold R.Osts that are spawned frequently. Although the Pure Gold R.Osts are [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, close-range [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]] and [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] are not recommended as the Pure Gold R.Osts will be able to reach them. If you happen to have any Critical Hitters with >260 range (like some of the  [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]] variants or [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]]), bringing them along would be a good idea. A particularly useful Critter here is [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]], who outranges Pure Gold R.Ost and will not target the [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] peons in the way. To beat the stage, bring along about 4 meatshields and then any other spammable/quickly-attacking unit with >260 range (ex. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]], etc.) that you have. The meatshields will hold the enemies back while the other units push forward. With the Pure Gold R.Osts' three knockbacks and low health, they should get pushed behind the base and then it should be an easy win from there.

